      "id": "90af8d1e-ace3-4fad-ae7e-30ec549a5fe6",
      "body": "The `model:` section in `configs/config_script.yaml` (lines 108-147) fully defines the backbone architecture, the fine-tuning head, and the LoRA setup \u2014 and the notebook consumes it directly rather than hardcoding any of these values:\n\n**Backbone architecture** (`img_size` through `time_embedding`) \u2014 passed to `HelioSpectformer1D.from_config(cfg.model, ...)` in cell `d1941589`. These must match the pretrained checkpoint's shape (`embed_dim: 1280`, `depth: 10`, `patch_size: 16`, etc.) since cell `fccfff48` then loads `surya.366m.v1.pt` weights into that architecture \u2014 mismatched dims here would cause the \"low tensor match count\" warning `load_pretrained_weights()` reports.\n\n**Fine-tuning head** (`pooling`, `penultimate_linear_layer`, `dropout`) \u2014 controls the task-specific head that projects the backbone's output down to your 1 regression value (flare/event score).\n\n**Fine-tuning regime** (`freeze_backbone`, `use_lora`, `lora_config`) \u2014 read in cell `677a4319` to pick one of three regimes documented in CLAUDE.md: LoRA (default here), linear probe, or full fine-tune. This is what the \"Trainable parameters\" printout in that cell reflects.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: your `lora_config.target_modules` is currently `[q_proj, v_proj, k_proj, out_proj, fc1, fc2]` (line 147), but per CLAUDE.md this backbone fuses q/k/v into a single `attn.qkv` Linear and names its output projection `attn.proj` \u2014 there's no `q_proj`/`k_proj`/`v_proj`/`out_proj` anywhere in the model. PEFT only raises when *no* target matches at all, so since `fc1`/`fc2` do match, this silently adapts only the FFN layers and skips attention entirely \u2014 the trainable-parameter count would be lower than expected and attention wouldn't get any LoRA adapters. If you want attention adapted too, it should be `[fc1, fc2, attn.qkv, attn.proj]` (the dotted form matters, since a bare `proj` would also match the patch-embedding Conv2d).",
